  "answer": "### Short Answer\nAn individual with ₱250,000 gross compensation income in 2024 is not required to file an income tax return. This is because the income is within the tax-exempt threshold set by the law.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThe relevant provision is found in Section 24 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which states that individuals with gross income not exceeding ₱250,000 are exempt from income tax.\n\n### Interpretation\nAccording to Section 24 of the NIRC, the income tax rates for individuals specify that for the taxable year 2023 and onwards, individuals earning not over ₱250,000 are subject to a 0% tax rate. Therefore, if an individual's gross compensation income is exactly ₱250,000, they fall within this exemption threshold.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nAs a result, individuals earning ₱250,000 or less from compensation income are not required to file an income tax return, provided that their income is solely from one employer and the correct amount of tax has been withheld. This simplifies compliance for low-income earners, allowing them to avoid the administrative burden of filing a return.",
